# Aleph: discover a relational rule, then watch it overfit

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:swi_elixir, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)},
  {:kino, "== 0.19.0"}
])
```

## Introduction

A train has several cars, and each car has properties. Can a learner explain
which trains are eastbound? Does its rule work on a train it has never seen?
This chapter uses the real [Aleph learner](https://github.com/friguzzi/aleph)
to discover a relational classifier, deliberately force memorization, and
learn recursive list membership.

Evaluate top to bottom in a local runtime on a [supported platform](../README.md#platforms-and-native-bundles).
Setup installs this checkout, its bundled SWI runtime, and Kino. The learner
is vendored, and all task source and training data is inline below. Start with
[Getting started](01_basic.livemd) for the wrapper or [Metagol](05_metagol.livemd)
for another approach to Inductive Logic Programming.

[All chapters](intro.livemd).

